// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  DSA paged-MQA gated top-k logits (gfx942), issue #51. See dsa.hpp for the
//  gated-logit formula and the paged-KV tensor layout.
//
//  Why this exists: tilelang_fp8_paged_mqa_logits JIT-compiles on gfx942 but
//  the launched kernel never returns (silent hang) for num_heads in {32,64};
//  deep_gemm.fp8_paged_mqa_logits is CUDA-only (NameError on HIP). This is the
//  plain gfx942 replacement -- the simple, correct baseline (one lane per
//  key, sequential H-sum, K staged once per page and reused across all H
//  heads), the topk's counterpart to dsa_sparse_fwd's "one query row per
//  wavefront, one key at a time". A tiled-key / MFMA-fp8 prefetch is a
//  follow-on optimisation, not required for correctness.
//
//  Mapping: one wavefront (B lanes) per (batch, split_kv) block. Each lane
//  owns ONE KV token (j = lane) within the current page and writes
//  out[b, i*B + lane] = sKscale[lane] * acc (guarded by t < seq_len[b];
//  tokens >= seq_len[b] are left unwritten -- the caller zeroes the output).
//
//  Paging: np_total = ceildiv(seq_len[b], B) pages are split across split_kv
//  blocks via stride = ceildiv(np_total, split_kv); block pid_split owns
//  [i_start, i_start + n_iters). split_kv is a PERF knob only -- the grouped
//  logit is grouping-independent (mirrors dsa_sparse_fwd's block_I/inner_iter).
//
//  LDS (one block): Q (H*D fp32) + gate (H fp32) once per block; per page
//  one K tile (B*D fp8->fp32) + B per-token scales (fp32, packed in the
//  trailing B*4 bytes of each B*(D+4) KV block). Total = (H*D + H + B*D + B)*4
//  = 49,536 B at the GLM-5.3 config (H=32, D=128, B=64) -- under the 64 KB
//  non-optin cap, so NO hipFuncSetAttribute opt-in (unlike MHC's 256 KB).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
```

